# Cursor rules for Anima-Protocol monorepo

## Scope
You are working in a monorepo:
- frontend: artifacts/anima-protocol
- api server: artifacts/api-server
- shared packages/libs: lib/*

## Code style
- Prefer existing patterns and utilities in the repo.
- Keep changes minimal and localized.
- Use TypeScript where the target file is TS/TSX; otherwise preserve JS where it already exists.

## Voice / Speak-to-Anima integration
- Any "Speak to Anima" UI wiring must pass through the existing components/hooks:
  - components/chat/SpeakToAnimaFunctionality.jsx
  - components/anima/SpeakToAnimaButton.jsx
  - hooks/useSpeakToAnima.js
  - components/voice/speakToAnima.js
- Do not hardcode ElevenLabs API keys in client code.
- If a server endpoint is required, implement it under artifacts/api-server and call it from the client.

## Testing
- If you modify frontend logic, run:
  - pnpm -C artifacts/anima-protocol test
  - pnpm -C artifacts/anima-protocol typecheck
- If you modify api server logic, run:
  - pnpm -C artifacts/api-server test
  - pnpm -C artifacts/api-server typecheck
- If you make integration changes, run top-level build:
  - pnpm build

## Git hygiene
- Do not remove existing functionality.
- Ensure formatting/linting does not break.

